            TODOs, FIXMEs, XXXs, and general notes and ideas

§ Generate manuals automatically

Both xmenu(1) and ctrlmenu(3) has two sections in common:
§USAGE and §RESOURCES.  Rather than edit both files and keep them in
sync, use some preprocessor or ed script to generate them from a common
file for those sections.


§ Implement ctrlmenu_radial(), make πmenu(1) based on ctrlmenu(3)

Implement a ctrlmenu_radial() for pop-up pie menus; and rewrite πmenu(1)
to use the ctrlmenu library underneath.


§ Pass processed resources to routines, rather than raw resource database

ctrlmenu_popup() and related routines get a XrmDatabase parameter, after
which the color, font, dimensions and other resources are read and
computed every time those routines are called.

It should be better to compute the resources once and pass them to each
routine.


§ Re-implement percent geometry(?)

xmenu(1) is a pop-up menu, which opens next to the mouse cursor.
But i have spotted a few people using it as a dmenu-but-for-mouse,
and want to pop-up the root menu at the center of the monitor.

I implemented a XParseGeometry(3)-compatible geometry parsed with
extensions for setting placement based on monitor size.

I am not sure whether i should re-implement it before a major release.


§ Remove scroll buttons when fully scrolled

When at the top, do not draw scroll-up button.
When at the bottom, do not draw scroll-down button.
